# === AI / Tooling ===
# `.claude/skills/` IS committed — the roadkeep skill is a vendored copy that
# `roadkeep install --check` keeps in step with the checkout it came from.
# Everything else under .claude/ is local machine state: locks, scheduled-task
# bookkeeping. Note the `*` — git does not descend into an ignored directory, so
# `/.claude/` without it would make the negations below unreachable.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
# settings.json IS committed: it declares the roadkeep marketplace and enables the
# plugin, so a clone gets the hook, the tools and the skill with no local setup.
!/.claude/settings.json
# hooks/ IS committed: the plugin never installs on Claude Code on the web (no
# `/plugin`), so the committed roadkeep-launch.py is how a cloud session gets the
# guard the plugin would give a local machine.
!/.claude/hooks/
# `roadkeep report` output — a local capture, never a source.
.roadkeep/

# === Test-guest credentials ===
# `scripts/vm.ps1` reads DOCKERDESK_* from environment variables or from a file *outside* this
# repository, so nothing here should ever hold one. This is the net for one written in here by
# mistake — a committed credential cannot be un-published by deleting it later.
*.env

# === .NET ===
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user
.vs/

# === Build output ===
/dist/
